dialect grammar
grammar raster.document.diff
extension raster
use family-scene
start diff

# HONEST BOUNDARY: no text (or binary) codec exists for `RasterDiff` — there is no real syntax to
# transcribe, so this grammar intentionally defines no body production beyond this notice (per
# the STUBS-AND-PLACEHOLDERS-COMPLETION ticket's brief: "do NOT invent a grammar" when the Rust
# genuinely has no parser). This REPLACES the stale, cross-plugin copy-pasted "canvas layer"
# template (`add-layer`/`remove-layer`/`move id=... dx=... dy=...`) this file previously carried,
# which was equally fictional — raster's diff apply/absorb logic never had a text form either.
#
# Evidence:
# - `RasterDiff` (🧬️schema/🔺️diff/🦀️component.rs:9-46) derives only `ArtifactSchema` — never
#   `dsl::DslDiff`. Compare the two derive expansions: `expand_dsl_diff`
#   (🧰️framework/🛍️products/💻️os/🔨️modules/🗣️dsl/✨️derive/🦀️component.rs:1419-1473) generates a real
#   `print_diff`/`parse_diff`/`encode_diff`/`decode_diff` (`DiffCodec`) impl; `expand_artifact_schema`
#   (🧰️framework/🔨️modules/🧬️schema/✨️derive/🦀️component.rs:201-260) generates only
#   `field_states()` — schema introspection, no serialization at all.
# - This facet's own `📝️text/🦀️component.rs` (🧬️schema/🔺️diff/📝️text/🦀️component.rs, 463 lines) has
#   no `impl store::ArtifactDsl`/`OpText`/`DiffText for RasterDiff` anywhere — only in-memory Rust
#   builder functions (`diff_add_layer`/`diff_remove_layer`/`diff_patch_layer`/`diff_move_layer`/
#   `diff_add_asset`/`diff_remove_asset`, lines 429-459) that construct a `RasterDiff` value
#   directly, and the semantic `MutationDiff<RasterSnapshot>::apply`/`absorb` trait impl
#   (lines 336-421) that merges/replays diffs already held in memory — neither reads or writes text.
# - `RasterDiff` DOES derive `Serialize`/`Deserialize` (plain serde JSON), but that is a different,
#   unrelated wire form from this `.grammar.semio`'s subject (the handcrafted `.raster` DSL text
#   grammar family every OTHER facet in this ticket documents) and is not transcribed here either.
diff = unimplemented-notice
unimplemented-notice = "NO-TEXT-CODEC-EXISTS-FOR-THIS-FACET"
